Flow Programming Language v2.0.0

Usage: flow [OPTIONS] <program.flow>

Options:
  run <program> [--backend=c|mlir] [--sanitize=ub,asan,tsan] [--profile=safety]
                    Compile and run program
  compile <program> [--backend=c|mlir] [--sanitize=...] [--profile=safety] [--show-flags]
                    Compile program only; --show-flags prints clang flags
  show-flags [--profile=safety] [--sanitize=...]  Print clang CFLAGS for current profile
  analyze <file.c> [--standard=misra-c-2024|cert-c] [--fail-on-violation]
                    Scan generated C for MISRA/CERT patterns (#277)
  Compiler: flowc (compiler/src); FLOWC_BIN=<path> picks a flowc binary
  CPU backend: FLOW_CPU_BACKEND=c|mlir or --backend= (default c; mlir needs LLVM)
  C flags: -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra (MISRA Phase 0); FLOW_PROFILE=safety adds -Werror
  Sanitizers: FLOW_UBSAN=1 FLOW_ASAN=1 FLOW_TSAN=1 or FLOW_SANITIZE=ub,asan,tsan
  audio <program> [--mlir]   Compile and run with audio backend
  compile-audio <program> [--mlir]  Compile with audio backend
  debug <program> [--break N|--break main] [--no-launch]  Debug build (+ optional LLDB/GDB)
  window <program>  Run with SDL2 window backend
  gfx <program>     Run with native FLOW gfx backend (macOS/Linux/Windows via SDL2)
  record <program> [--frames N] [--skip N] [--out DIR] [--gif [PATH]] [--keys SPEC] [--mouse SPEC]
                   [--fps N] [--stride N] [--width PX]
                    Run a gfx program headless; write PPM frames, or a GIF with --gif
  shader <program>  Run fill-shader demo (Metal window on macOS; --emit-only, --wgsl; see docs/language/shaders.md)
  demo vulkan [basic|advanced]  Vulkan triangle / scene demos (macOS + MoltenVK)
  demo vulkan-flow [basic|advanced|2048|tetris|snake|pong|breakout|layout|layout-dsl]
  demo ui-layout[|-window]  UI layout demos (SDL2 for -window)
  Compat aliases (same as demo …): vulkan-demo[-basic|-advanced], vulkan-2048,
    vulkan-tetris, vulkan-snake, vulkan-pong, vulkan-breakout,
    vulkan-layout[-dsl], ui-layout[-window]
  mlir <program> [flags]  Generate MLIR (pass --optimize / --opt-level / --no-*)
  mlir-run <program> Compile via MLIR and run
  fir-g <program>    Dump FIR-G graph + analyses; --calibrate / --opts
  jit <program>      JIT compile and run (fastest)
  ml [run|jit|bench|test] [program]  MLIR-first ML workloads (tensors, matmul)
  gpu <program>      Generate @gpu compute kernels as Metal sources
  shader <program>   Run fill-shader demo (Metal; macOS)
  explain <program>  Print the compilation plan for every declarative
                    construct: implementations considered, their costs,
                    the choice, and what each rejected candidate failed
                    (flowc with FLOWC_EXPLAIN=1)
  transpile <program> [args...]  Run the Python MLIR transpiler (advanced flags)
  fmt [--check] <files...>  Format FLOW source files in place
                    (--check: list files that would change, exit 1)

Testing:
  test [flags]      Run FLOW tests (flowc + clang validate)
                    --strict    Fail on type errors
                    --lenient   Warnings only (default)
                    --tier1     Transpile only (fast)
                    --tier2     Transpile + clang (default)
                    --verbose   Show error details
                    --sanitize=ub,asan,tsan  Enable sanitizers for compile/run tests
  test-strict       Shortcut for: test --strict
  test-runtime      Run runtime tests (compile + execute)
  test-lang         Run tests/lang/ language tests (strict flowc + compile + execute)
  test-mlir         Run MLIR verification (requires LLVM)
  test-scripts      Run the shell tests in tests/scripts
  test-interop      Run interop runtime tests
  test-gpu          Run GPU feature + codegen tests
  test-matmul       Run matmul optimization demo + print assembly
  test-all          Run FLOW + Python tests

Project / packages:
  init [name]       Initialize a new project (flow.toml)
  add <package>     Add dependency (name, name@^1.0, --git, --path)
  patch <file.flow>  Compile and run a corpus patch smoke harness
  sync [--program FILE]  Synchronize the nearest project's dependencies
  pkg install       Install flow.toml dependencies → flow_packages/
  search [query]    Search the Flow package registry
  info <package>    Show package versions / source
  publish           Register package in local registry/index.json
  build             Build the project
  build-native      Build with native sources (uses flow.toml)
  run-native        Build and run with native sources
  clean             Clean build artifacts
  install           Install project deps if flow.toml exists; else LLVM tools
  setup             Install LLVM / compiler tooling
  python <program>  Generate Python package (wheel)
  wasm <program> [--backend=c|mlir] [--preload DIR@/MOUNT] [--link PATH]
                    [--threads] [--fs memfs|idbfs] [--out DIR]
                    Compile to WebAssembly + a runnable page
  wasm32 <in.flow|in.ll> -o OUT.wasm [--export NAME] [-O O0..Oz]
                    Freestanding wasm32 module through MLIR (no libc)
  bpf <in.flow|in.ll> -o OUT.o [--entry NAME --section SEC] [-O 0..3]
                    eBPF ELF object (bpfel) through MLIR
  repl              Start interactive REPL
  lsp               Start the language server on stdio
  examples          List project examples (or compiler examples outside a project)
  examples run NAME Run a packaged project example from the current root
  playground        Start native-local compile API + open playground docs
  dap <file>        Debug Adapter (IDE) / opens flow debug on TTY
  version           Print Flow version (2.0.0)
  help              Show this help

Environment:
  FLOW_STRICT_EFFECTS=1  Abort on unhandled effect ops (C backend)
                         Also enables compile-time effect-row checks with --strict-effects
  FLOW_CPU_BACKEND=c|mlir  Select CPU codegen (default c; same as --backend)
  FLOWC_BIN=<path>       flowc binary for the C path (default: built from compiler/bootstrap)

Examples:
  flow run examples/fibonacci.flow
  flow run --backend=mlir examples/basics/hello_world.flow
  flow compile examples/loops.flow
  flow test --strict --verbose
  flow test-runtime --verbose
  flow test-interop
  flow test-gpu --verbose
  flow test-matmul [--no-asm] [--no-mlir]
